<style lang="scss">
  .deskart {
    display: block;
    // A cut-out stands a few millimetres off the page and throws a hard
    // offset, not a photographic blur. TreeLine.astro's trees are lit the
    // same way, and so is the desk itself. The offset paints outside this
    // element's own box — an SVG filter result is not clipped by the root's
    // overflow — which is why not one of the four drawings is allowed to
    // spend its last two units of the 120 box: whatever else it lands beside
    // on the desk, it must not land on top of it.
    filter: drop-shadow(3px 5px 0 var(--sh-1));
  }

  // The garments on the rail and the letter's flag are the only things on the
  // desk that move. Barely a degree, once every nine seconds — the same size
  // of sway TreeLine.astro gives the trees, and for the same reason: enough
  // to read as hung up, not enough to pull an eye off the words beside it.
  // Anyone who has asked their system for less motion gets none of it.
  .art-sway {
    transform-box: fill-box;
    transform-origin: 50% 0%;

    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
      animation: deskart-sway 9s $ease-paper infinite;
      animation-delay: var(--sway-delay, 0s);
    }
  }

  @keyframes deskart-sway {
    0%, 100% { transform: rotate(-1.1deg); }
    50%      { transform: rotate(1.1deg); }
  }
</style>
